diff --git a/PC98-PORT.md b/PC98-PORT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b579765
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PC98-PORT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# Legacy i386 maintenance notes
+
+## Upstream base
+
+- Project: musl libc
+- Release: 1.2.6
+- Source: `https://musl.libc.org/releases/musl-1.2.6.tar.gz`
+- SHA-256:
+  `d585fd3b613c66151fc3249e8ed44f77020cb5e6c1e635a616d3f9f82460512a`
+
+The upstream release was imported without generated build files. The local
+source changes represented by the initial import are also preserved as:
+
+- `patches/musl-1.2.6-i386-tas-lock.patch`
+- `patches/musl-1.2.6-i386-static-profile.patch`
+
+Those patches are provenance records only. The source in this directory is
+the build input and the authoritative maintained version.
+
+## Local scope
+
+The i386 internal lock uses a three-state test-and-set implementation based
+on memory `LOCK XCHG` and futex wait/wake. It implements the locking
+contract directly and is not a compare-and-exchange emulation.
+
+The `MUSL_I386_SINGLE_THREAD` and `MUSL_NO_FLOAT` macros select the
+low-memory static BusyBox profile. They avoid linking unsupported pthread
+atomic paths and floating-point stdio into that image. They are not a claim
+that the complete musl pthread API has been ported to an i386.
+
+## Updating from upstream
+
+For a new musl release:
+
+1. Record the release URL, version, SHA-256, and upstream tag or commit.
+2. Import the pristine release separately from local changes so the
+   upstream delta remains reviewable.
+3. Merge the upstream changes into this directory; do not reapply the old
+   1.2.6 patch files blindly.
+4. Build both the normal upstream-compatible configuration and the PC-98
+   low-memory profile.
+5. Scan the final i386 binary for post-i386 instructions.
+6. Boot qemu-pc98 with `-cpu 386`, mount ext4, enable swap, and reach the
+   static BusyBox shell.
+7. Run the test-and-set contention test and confirm its final counter and
+   lock state.
+
+Preserve the upstream `COPYRIGHT` file and document every local behavioral
+change here.
